abstract: |
  Standard gravitational lensing analysis relies on the Isochrony Axiom—the implicit assumption that the observed image represents a synchronous spatial snapshot of the source. For evolving sources, this approximation breaks down in the presence of conformal metric couplings, creating a "temporal composite" image. This projects temporal depth onto the spatial plane, generating a temporal-composite response contribution sourced by the underlying Temporal Shear field gradient—arising from gradients in the scalar field's continuous spatial profile (Temporal Topology, TEP)—whose propagating component is confined to the millisecond (conservative-baseline) window while its chronometric component is bounded by the ratio of differential delay to source-evolution time and is accessible only through time-domain or variability-dependent observables. Within TEP, Phantom Mass is the excess dynamical mass inferred when the scalar force on matter trajectories is analyzed as gravitating mass. Its test is the mass difference inferred from dynamics and lensing at matched radii and with compatible mass models. Whereas isotropic conformal rescaling g̃_μν=A²(φ)g_μν stretches spatial rulers alongside clocks so A²(φ(x)) cancels out of null rays, under the canonical unstretched-space temporal metric g̃_μν=-A_loc²(u_grav(x))U_μ U_ν+Aₛₚ²(u_drift(t,x))Π_μν (U_μ≡-∇_μφ̄/√(2X̄)) the (3+1) ADM spacetime lapse rescales as N_TEP(x)=A(φ(x))N_GR(x) while the spatial 3-metric γ_ij remains unstretched. Intermediate clock rates along the ray therefore contribute -β_A u_grav(x) directly to the optical refractive index n(x)≃1-2Φ_N(x)/c²-β_A u_grav(x), preserving local Lorentz invariance and c_GW=c_γ identically on the shared temporal-lapse cone (Δ t_γ-GW=0). Sourced by baryons alone on the selected kinetic sector P_,X=k√ξ+2ξ (k=16.03 fixed by a₀, zero per-system free parameters), this unstretched-space temporal refraction reproduces the Bullet Cluster galaxy-peak convergence and offset morphology (κₜₒₜ=0.307–0.372 at the bullet galaxies, peak at x=+0.352 Mpc on the galaxies, no negative moat; Step 02) without particulate dark matter, consistent with the companion strong-lensing delay and CMB lensing closures (Papers 18, 19).
  Screening of the shear response in high-acceleration lensing environments is governed by the abstract environmental operator 𝒮_Σ(ℰ), which pins the incremental field gradient where the ambient landscape is steep while the Temporal Topology persists. The same operator sets the environment-dependence of the phantom mass, which is accordingly largest in isolated, diffuse low-acceleration systems.
